'''Warda Gojun''', designated "'''HH-4413'''," was a [[human]] [[Homeworld|native]] of the [[planet]] [[Saleucami]]. By [[1 BBY]], he held the [[Military rank|rank]] of [[sergeant]] in the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Imperial Army]] and was stationed in [[Jedha City]], where he served as a member of a [[TX-225 GAVw "Occupier" combat assault tank|tank]] crew commanded by [[First Sergeant]] [[Jimmon Arbmab]]. Before the Empire evacuated from Jedha, Gojun and his crew were involved in a deadly ambush by local [[partisans]] which left Arbmab and many other Imperial [[Soldier|personnel]] [[Death|dead]].

==Biography==
===Early life and pre-deployment===
Warda Gojun was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] individual who was [[Reproduction|born]]<ref name="UVG" /> on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Saleucami]]<ref name="Saleucami">{{Databank|saleucami|Saleucami}}</ref> around [[23 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> and joined the [[Galactic Empire]]<ref name="UVG" /> before or during [[1 BBY]]<ref name="Timelines" /> and subsequently given the designation "HH-4413". Gojun was eventually promoted to the [[Military rank|rank]] of [[sergeant]] and assigned to the [[Imperial Army]]'s [[71st GAV Battalion]] under the command of [[First Sergeant]] [[Jimmon Arbmab]].<ref name="UVG" />

===Skirmish in Jedha City===
{{Quote|Roll forward. Crush everything ahead of us.|First Sergeant Jimmon Arbmab|<ref name="UVG" />}}
[[File:Imperial_Hovertank_on_Jedha.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The Imperial tank proceeds through the enclosed Jedha streets]]
The 22 [[Standard year|year]]<ref name="Date" /> old trooper and his [[TX-225 GAVw "Occupier" combat assault tank|tank]] crew were deployed to the [[desert]] [[moon]] of [[Jedha]], and shortly before the Empire's evacuation were assigned to a transport detail for [[kyber crystal]]s being exported off of the moon from [[Jedha City]].<ref name="UVG" /> The [[Hovertank|tank]] was escorted by a [[squad]] of heavily armed [[stormtrooper]]s, and proceeded carefully along their route through the cities narrow, enclosed streets&mdash;streets that were strategically ideal for ambushes. Nonetheless, the transport detail moved through the city, wary of hostile forces.<ref name="Rogue One" />

Despite their concern, the escort was swiftly ambushed by local [[partisans]] affiliated with [[Saw Gerrera]] while they proceeded along their route. The escort responded in turn and inflicted heavy [[Death|casualties]] on the insurgents, and Gojun, along with his crew, delivered several deadly shots into the insurgents' ambush positions. Despite the efforts of the escort team, the stormtrooper escort was eliminated after the brutal firefight. In the chaos, Arbmab, Gojun's commanding officer, was killed by a point-blank shot from [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] [[spy]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]]. The tank exploded due to a Partisan, and Gojun was [[Death|killed]] in the chaos.<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Personality and traits==
Gojun was a human [[Gender|male]] native to Saleucami, and stood 1.81 [[meter]]s (5 [[Foot|feet]], 9 inches) tall.<ref name="UVG" />

==Equipment==
Gojun wore the [[Color|white]] [[plastoid]] [[armor]] of an Imperial tank trooper, and was equipped with compact repair and diagnostic kits affixed to his [[belt]]. Additionally, his [[helmet]] was furnished with a wireless telemetry receiver, which connected to the tank system interfaces.<ref name="UVG" />

==Behind the scenes==
Warda Gojun first appeared in the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Star Wars Anthology'']] film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="Rogue One" /> and Gojun's name was established simultaneously in the reference book ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]].''<ref name="UVG" /> An error occurs in the film in which Gojun and Arbmab's bodies disappear when the tank is being blown up by a Partisan.<ref name="Rogue One" /> The same happens in the [[Rogue One Adaptation 2|''Rogue One Adaptation'']], in which Gojun disappears after appearing in one frame.<ref name="Adaptation">[[Rogue One Adaptation 2|''Rogue One Adaptation'' 2]]</ref>

